WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.251 --> 00:00:01.418
coverage today from east

00:00:01.552 --> 00:00:02.720
Lansing, where the first victims

00:00:02.853 --> 00:00:04.822
of yesterday's horrific attack

00:00:04.955 --> 00:00:08.259
have been identified.

00:00:08.392 --> 00:00:10.394
&gt;&gt; Really multiple ambulances.

00:00:10.527 --> 00:00:11.996
&gt;&gt; Reporter: The shootings at

00:00:12.129 --> 00:00:12.730
Michigan state university left

00:00:12.863 --> 00:00:15.332
three students dead and five

00:00:15.466 --> 00:00:16.166
others critically injured.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:24.074
Brian Fraser, a sophomore,verner, were among

00:00:24.208 --> 00:00:26.944
those killed.

00:00:27.077 --> 00:00:28.145
Anthony Mcrae first opened fire

00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:30.214
on the campus Monday just before

00:00:30.347 --> 00:00:30.581
8:30 P.M.

00:00:30.714 --> 00:00:31.916
&gt;&gt; Oh, my god.

00:00:31.916 --> 00:00:32.950
&gt;&gt; There's still people trying

00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:33.951
to get out.

00:00:34.084 --> 00:00:37.121
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Shooting at two

00:00:37.254 --> 00:00:38.756
locations, the first inside a

00:00:38.889 --> 00:00:39.123
classroom.

00:00:39.256 --> 00:00:41.358
&gt;&gt; While the officers were

00:00:41.492 --> 00:00:42.493
managing that scene at the hall,

00:00:42.626 --> 00:00:44.261
we began receiving additional

00:00:44.395 --> 00:00:47.932
reports of another shooting at

00:00:47.932 --> 00:00:49.934
the msu union building.

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:51.969
&gt;&gt; I'm coming down.

00:00:52.102 --> 00:00:52.770
Seven people.

00:00:52.903 --> 00:00:54.104
&gt;&gt; Reporter: One witness to the

00:00:54.238 --> 00:00:56.040
shooting says his

00:00:56.173 --> 00:00:57.074
fight-or-flight response kicked

00:00:57.207 --> 00:00:57.341
in.

00:00:57.474 --> 00:00:59.009
&gt;&gt; I went to the far side of the

00:00:59.143 --> 00:01:01.045
class and ducked down, and he

00:01:01.178 --> 00:01:03.948
came in and shot three to four

00:01:03.981 --> 00:01:05.316
times in our classroom.

00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:06.784
&gt;&gt; Police released a photo of

00:01:06.917 --> 00:01:08.419
the shooter taken from campus

00:01:08.552 --> 00:01:11.155
security cameras and a caller's

00:01:11.288 --> 00:01:14.491
tip sent them to Lansing,

00:01:14.625 --> 00:01:17.528
Michigan.

00:01:17.962 --> 00:01:23.334
The search ended just before

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:24.001
midnight.

00:01:24.134 --> 00:01:25.336
Police say Mcrae shot himself

00:01:25.469 --> 00:01:28.238
during a confrontation and died.

00:01:28.372 --> 00:01:32.209
He had no known motive to target

00:01:32.343 --> 00:01:34.211
msu and no ties to the

00:01:34.345 --> 00:01:34.611
university.

00:01:34.745 --> 00:01:35.646
According to police, they're now

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:37.214
investigating a two-page note

00:01:37.348 --> 00:01:39.016
found in Mcrae's backpack,

00:01:39.149 --> 00:01:40.751
saying he's going to, quote,

00:01:40.884 --> 00:01:42.353
finish off Lansing and that

00:01:42.486 --> 00:01:44.655
there are, quote, 20 of him who

00:01:44.788 --> 00:01:46.390
will carry out shootings

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:47.124
according to a source familiar

00:01:47.257 --> 00:01:48.625
with the investigation.

00:01:48.759 --> 00:01:50.027
Mcrae had been arrested before.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:51.996
He was released from probation

00:01:52.029 --> 00:01:54.198
in may of 2021 after pleading

00:01:54.331 --> 00:01:56.000
guilty to a misdemeanor for

00:01:56.066 --> 00:01:59.536
possession of a loaded firearm.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:00.704
Msu students are now dealing

00:02:00.838 --> 00:02:02.272
with what's next after spending

00:02:02.406 --> 00:02:05.209
hours hiding from a gunman.

00:02:05.342 --> 00:02:06.610
&gt;&gt; We took heavy furniture from

00:02:06.744 --> 00:02:10.347
around the library and just

00:02:10.481 --> 00:02:11.181
barricaded ourselves into a

00:02:11.315 --> 00:02:14.651
study room to make sure we were

00:02:14.785 --> 00:02:14.952
safe.

00:02:15.085 --> 00:02:15.686
&gt;&gt; I was, like, shaking in the

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:16.687
bathroom, and it was just

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:17.054
terrible.

00:02:17.187 --> 00:02:18.522
Just, like, preparing myself

00:02:18.655 --> 00:02:19.556
for, like, the worst thing ever.

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:21.358
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Despite the tough

00:02:21.492 --> 00:02:24.028
circumstances, there's one

00:02:24.028 --> 00:02:26.764
greeting among all Spartans that

00:02:26.897 --> 00:02:27.364
still unites them.

00:02:27.498 --> 00:02:30.401
&gt;&gt; Go, green!

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:31.235
&gt;&gt; Go, green!

00:02:31.368 --> 00:02:32.302
&gt;&gt; Reporter: You smiled

00:02:32.436 --> 00:02:32.669
instantly.

00:02:32.803 --> 00:02:34.038
&gt;&gt; As horrible and disgusting

00:02:34.071 --> 00:02:36.040
and tragic as that was, we are

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:36.573
all in it together and everyone

00:02:36.707 --> 00:02:39.443
was here for each other.

00:02:39.576 --> 00:02:41.612
&gt;&gt; Reporter: That's the greeting

00:02:42.046 --> 00:02:43.347
every freshman learns at

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:44.782
orientation, and today it

00:02:44.915 --> 00:02:46.050
provided a moment of comfort for

00:02:46.116 --> 00:02:47.117
those hurting students,

00:02:47.251 --> 00:02:48.752
especially as they learn more

00:02:48.886 --> 00:02:50.454
about this 43-year-old shooter.

00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:53.023
His father spoke to CNN, telling

00:02:53.157 --> 00:02:55.092
us his son changed about two

00:02:55.225 --> 00:02:57.094
years ago when his mother died

00:02:57.227 --> 00:02:58.062
following a stroke.

00:02:58.095 --> 00:03:00.898
He said his son became isolated,

00:03:01.031 --> 00:03:04.168
bitter, and, quote, evil angry.

00:03:04.301 --> 00:03:04.735
Jake?

00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:06.070
&gt;&gt; Adrienne Broaddus in east

00:03:06.203 --> 00:03:10.174
Lansing, Michigan, for us.

00:03:10.307 --> 00:03:12.076
Elissa Slotkin of Michigan joins

00:03:12.209 --> 00:03:16.814
me from the university.

00:03:16.947 --> 00:03:18.082
She Lansing and

00:03:18.182 --> 00:03:19.183
the campus.

00:03:19.316 --> 00:03:20.651
Congresswoman, I'm angry we're

00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:21.718
having this conversation again.

00:03:22.086 --> 00:03:24.188
I'm sure you are too.

00:03:24.321 --> 00:03:24.922
This is the second mass shooting

00:03:25.055 --> 00:03:26.990
at a school in your area in the

00:03:27.124 --> 00:03:29.259
last year and a half, the first

00:03:29.393 --> 00:03:30.594
oxford high school in 2021.

00:03:30.727 --> 00:03:31.295
First, how is your community

00:03:31.428 --> 00:03:37.267
doing today?

00:03:37.401 --> 00:03:38.469
&gt;&gt; Yeah, well.

00:03:38.602 --> 00:03:40.270
Look, it's the first day after a

00:03:40.404 --> 00:03:40.971
huge trauma.

00:03:41.105 --> 00:03:42.306
You know, for a while it was

00:03:42.439 --> 00:03:44.108
just a very quiet and empty

00:03:44.108 --> 00:03:45.109
place, the campus.

00:03:45.242 --> 00:03:48.846
Kids were really holed up in

00:03:48.979 --> 00:03:49.580
their dorm rooms, in apartments.

00:03:49.713 --> 00:03:51.782
We were making sure kids were

00:03:52.116 --> 00:03:52.883
together, they had someone else

00:03:53.016 --> 00:03:53.650
to be with.

00:03:53.784 --> 00:03:54.852
We're starting to see a few

00:03:54.985 --> 00:03:56.320
folks come out and want to be

00:03:56.453 --> 00:03:56.954
together.

00:03:57.087 --> 00:03:59.423
They're planning vigils, taking

00:03:59.556 --> 00:04:00.491
action, planning protests.

00:04:00.624 --> 00:04:01.792
They're starting to come out,

00:04:02.126 --> 00:04:03.227
but it is particularly because

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:04.862
it wasn't just a shooting, it

00:04:04.995 --> 00:04:07.331
was also a manhunt on campus.

00:04:07.464 --> 00:04:09.199
It was sort of a double trauma

00:04:09.333 --> 00:04:10.200
in a way.

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:12.703
And everyone felt the effects.

00:04:12.836 --> 00:04:14.271
Over 50,000 students are here,

00:04:14.404 --> 00:04:16.373
so it's a traumatic thing that

00:04:16.507 --> 00:04:18.142
will take a while to get over.

00:04:18.275 --> 00:04:19.743
&gt;&gt; Nothing could explain this

00:04:20.144 --> 00:04:22.146
madness, but have you learned

00:04:22.146 --> 00:04:24.748
anything about a possible

00:04:24.882 --> 00:04:25.082
motive?

00:04:25.215 --> 00:04:25.549
&gt;&gt; Reporter: No.

00:04:25.682 --> 00:04:27.284
I mean, I think to everyone's

00:04:27.417 --> 00:04:29.353
best estimate at this point is

00:04:29.486 --> 00:04:30.454
it was someone who was going

00:04:30.587 --> 00:04:32.756
through a real mental crisis.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:35.159
And, you know, by his own family

00:04:35.292 --> 00:04:37.561
admission, he was just

00:04:37.694 --> 00:04:38.495
struggling, and this person who

00:04:38.629 --> 00:04:39.563
was struggling with mental

00:04:39.696 --> 00:04:41.832
illness had access to a gun, had

00:04:42.166 --> 00:04:44.168
regular access to a gun.

00:04:44.301 --> 00:04:45.402
And, you know, we'll never I'm

00:04:45.536 --> 00:04:47.337
sure know exactly why he did it,

00:04:47.471 --> 00:04:48.739
but I think, you know, the thing

00:04:48.872 --> 00:04:51.008
that's just hard to ignore is

00:04:51.141 --> 00:04:52.943
how many times we've done this

00:04:53.076 --> 00:04:54.745
over the past just even year,

00:04:54.878 --> 00:04:56.880
year and a half.

00:04:57.014 --> 00:04:58.182
And, you know, are we willing to

00:04:58.215 --> 00:04:59.516
have an actual conversation

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:01.051
about doing something to

00:05:01.185 --> 00:05:02.886
mitigate these kind of gun

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:03.220
losses.

00:05:03.353 --> 00:05:05.155
It's been a frustrating day.

00:05:05.289 --> 00:05:08.192
You know, I'm not someone who

00:05:08.192 --> 00:05:09.359
usually fears -- feels-like fury

00:05:09.493 --> 00:05:10.627
about something, but having to

00:05:10.761 --> 00:05:15.265
talk to kids, I mean, you should

00:05:15.399 --> 00:05:16.733
have heard the conversations,

00:05:16.867 --> 00:05:18.202
talking to students.

00:05:18.268 --> 00:05:20.304
They were terrified, their

00:05:20.437 --> 00:05:21.505
parents were terrified.

00:05:21.638 --> 00:05:24.808
It's terrorizing, and we do

00:05:24.942 --> 00:05:26.243
something about something that's

00:05:26.376 --> 00:05:27.477
terrorizing our population or do

00:05:27.611 --> 00:05:27.811
nothing.

00:05:28.212 --> 00:05:28.612
That's the choice.

00:05:28.745 --> 00:05:30.214
&gt;&gt; So many shooters in the last

00:05:30.247 --> 00:05:33.116
few years have had run-ins with

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.851
the law or family members who

00:05:34.985 --> 00:05:36.220
said, yeah, he was really going

00:05:36.353 --> 00:05:38.589
through a tough time.

00:05:38.722 --> 00:05:40.224
This shooter's father says his

00:05:40.224 --> 00:05:41.725
son had a gun several years ago.

00:05:41.858 --> 00:05:44.228
Police took it away.

00:05:44.228 --> 00:05:45.362
Court documents show the gunman

00:05:45.495 --> 00:05:46.830
pleaded guilty to a firearms

00:05:46.964 --> 00:05:48.232
charge in 2019.

00:05:48.232 --> 00:05:50.734
And yet sources tell CNN this

00:05:50.867 --> 00:05:52.803
same person was able to purchase

00:05:52.936 --> 00:05:56.506
both guns in 2021.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:57.741
Is that legal in Michigan?

00:05:57.874 --> 00:06:01.011
Do we have any idea of whether

00:06:01.144 --> 00:06:01.745
this could have been stopped in

00:06:01.878 --> 00:06:03.880
any way, the purchasing?

00:06:04.248 --> 00:06:04.414
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Yeah.

00:06:04.548 --> 00:06:06.350
We really just don't know the

00:06:06.483 --> 00:06:07.484
full details yet.

00:06:07.618 --> 00:06:08.285
I don't want to speculate.

00:06:08.418 --> 00:06:09.286
I think, you know, the fact of

00:06:09.419 --> 00:06:11.521
the matter is we know it's a

00:06:11.655 --> 00:06:12.756
pretty high bar to get flagged

00:06:12.889 --> 00:06:15.492
when you're trying to purchase a

00:06:15.626 --> 00:06:15.826
weapon.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:17.928
And I don't know the

00:06:18.262 --> 00:06:19.563
circumstances of this man, but I

00:06:19.696 --> 00:06:21.164
know someone who's closest, you

00:06:21.298 --> 00:06:23.433
know, family felt that they were

00:06:23.567 --> 00:06:25.168
mentally unstable, had access to

00:06:25.302 --> 00:06:25.769
a weapon.

00:06:25.902 --> 00:06:27.304
I think one of the things that

00:06:27.437 --> 00:06:30.340
at least has made me feel a bit

00:06:30.474 --> 00:06:32.909
better is that we've had an

00:06:33.043 --> 00:06:34.945
outpouring of Michigan ganders.

00:06:35.078 --> 00:06:38.515
So many people here are Spartans

00:06:38.649 --> 00:06:41.885
and graduated or used to come by

00:06:42.286 --> 00:06:42.352
msu.

00:06:42.352 --> 00:06:44.688
There's a feeling you can be a

00:06:44.821 --> 00:06:46.890
gun owner, a sportsman, avrd

00:06:47.024 --> 00:06:48.358
hunter, grow up with weapons the

00:06:48.492 --> 00:06:51.028
way I did, and still believe in

00:06:51.161 --> 00:06:54.631
keeping kids safe in a place of

00:06:54.765 --> 00:06:55.232
sanctuary like a school.

00:06:55.365 --> 00:06:56.800
So, I think what has heartened

